### API Key Authentication Bypass in Development Environment
### 
### ✅ DEVELOPMENT MODE: API key authentication is bypassed for ALL routes
### When ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development (as in local docker setup)
### 
### You can now test ALL endpoints without providing API keys:

### 1. Test Logs API (previously required API key)
GET http://localhost:7071/api/logs
# No X-API-Key header needed in dev environment

### 2. Test Migration Status API
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/status
# No X-API-Key header needed in dev environment

### 3. Test Health Check (always open)
GET http://localhost:7071/api/health
# Always available regardless of environment

### 4. Test Debug Endpoints (always open)
GET http://localhost:7071/api/debug/info
# Always available regardless of environment

### ====================================
### ORIGINAL MIGRATION CANCELLATION TEST
### ====================================

### Test Migration Cancellation Flow
### This file demonstrates how to test the migration cancellation functionality

### 1. Start a Migration (replace with your actual migration request)
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceStore": {
    "storeId": "test-store",
    "apiUrl": "https://api.bigcommerce.com/stores/test-store/v3",
    "apiKey": "your-api-key"
  },
  "destinationStore": {
    "storeId": "dest-store", 
    "apiUrl": "https://api.bigcommerce.com/stores/dest-store/v3",
    "apiKey": "your-dest-api-key"
  },
  "entities": ["categories", "products"],
  "settings": {
    "batchSize": 10,
    "enableLogging": true
  }
}

### 2. Get Migration Status (use the migrationId from step 1)
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/status

### 3. Cancel Migration (use the migrationId from step 1)
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/cancel

### 4. Verify Cancellation - Check Status Again
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/status

### 5. Get Migration Logs (now works without API key in dev)
GET http://localhost:7071/api/logs?migrationId={{migrationId}}

### 6. Get All Migrations
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations

### 7. Get Migration History
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/history

### 8. Test with Real Migration ID
### Replace with actual migration ID from your system
@migrationId = 7a06c5b7-64c9-4c78-b687-f327b8ddc0d5

### Get specific migration details
GET http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}

### Cancel specific migration
POST http://localhost:7071/api/migrations/{{migrationId}}/cancel

### Get logs for specific migration
GET http://localhost:7071/api/logs?migrationId={{migrationId}}&level=info&limit=50

### Expected Behavior:
### 1. Migration should start successfully
### 2. Status should show "InProgress" 
### 3. After cancellation, status should show "Cancelled"
### 4. Logs should show cancellation messages
### 5. No API key required for any endpoint in Development environment 